From eb8753b1d90749a6e9bd149a5cc6a307a8ed6409 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sensa-code <255512260+sensa-code@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 17:46:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hayro: Support knockout groups

Objects in a transparency group with `/K true` were composited over each
other like in any other group. In a knockout group, each object is
composited with the initial backdrop of the group instead, so it replaces
the objects painted before it wherever it paints.

hayro-interpret now reads the `K` entry of transparency groups and pushes
knockout groups with the new `Device::push_knockout_group`. Its default
implementation calls `push_transparency_group`, so existing devices keep
working unchanged. The renderer in hayro draws paths and glyphs that are
painted directly into a knockout group with `Compose::Copy`: the layer of
the group starts out transparent, so this composites them with the initial
backdrop, and anti-aliased edges are interpolated by coverage.

Not covered yet: images and nested groups inside a knockout group are
still composited over the earlier objects, and a soft mask in the graphics
state acts as shape rather than opacity there. hayro-svg ignores the
attribute.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
